somebody you can trust,

3093
01:55:13.210 --> 01:55:15.040
somebody that you respect,

3094
01:55:15.040 --> 01:55:19.960
somebody that can provide you with solid counsel.

3095
01:55:19.960 --> 01:55:24.960
But I think the process of that communication is of itself,

3096
01:55:25.160 --> 01:55:26.880
a little bit of a letting go

3097
01:55:26.880 --> 01:55:30.910
and it will allow you to get a little more objectivity

3098
01:55:30.910 --> 01:55:32.190
on what's happening with you

3099
01:55:32.190 --> 01:55:33.940
to help you find the cause,

3100
01:55:33.940 --> 01:55:35.930
the triggers of those behaviors

3101
01:55:35.930 --> 01:55:39.340
that are sending you sideways and ultimately,

3102
01:55:39.340 --> 01:55:43.980
help you analyze this story that you're telling yourself,

3103
01:55:43.980 --> 01:55:46.820
that you're a failure and you can't help yourself

3104
01:55:46.820 --> 01:55:49.090
and everything's out of control,

3105
01:55:49.090 --> 01:55:50.770
to really deconstruct that

3106
01:55:50.770 --> 01:55:53.713
and perhaps construct a better, healthier,

3107
01:55:54.998 --> 01:55:57.240
less negative story for yourself.

3108
01:55:57.240 --> 01:55:58.513
You know, along the way,

3109
01:55:59.350 --> 01:56:02.630
can you find a way to listen to that,

3110
01:56:02.630 --> 01:56:04.790
you know, positive wolf, at all?

3111
01:56:04.790 --> 01:56:07.510
Can you make any kind of lifestyle adjustments

3112
01:56:08.370 --> 01:56:10.510
that would move you in a positive direction?

3113
01:56:10.510 --> 01:56:12.860
In recovery, they call it taking contrary action.

3114
01:56:12.860 --> 01:56:15.140
So when your instinct is, you know,

3115
01:56:15.140 --> 01:56:17.060
whether it's like, ah, I know I shouldn't drink

3116
01:56:17.060 --> 01:56:18.870
but I'm gonna take that drink, whatever it is,

3117
01:56:18.870 --> 01:56:20.480
like what is the contrary action?

3118
01:56:20.480 --> 01:56:22.490
Like, oh, I don't wanna pick up the phone

3119
01:56:22.490 --> 01:56:24.540
and tell that guy, what I just did.

3120
01:56:24.540 --> 01:56:26.260
The contrary action is to pick up the phone

3121
01:56:26.260 --> 01:56:28.000
and tell the guy what you did, right?

3122
01:56:28.000 --> 01:56:32.030
What is the smallest contrary action that you can take

3123
01:56:32.030 --> 01:56:34.850
that will break the seal on that and, you know,

3124
01:56:34.850 --> 01:56:38.019
initiate a different direction for yourself?

3125
01:56:38.019 --> 01:56:39.750
That's a great little,

3126
01:56:39.750 --> 01:56:42.170
super doable action step to do.

3127
01:56:42.170 --> 01:56:44.490
Like, if your mind is telling you one thing

3128
01:56:44.490 --> 01:56:46.210
and you know that's the negative thing,

3129
01:56:46.210 --> 01:56:47.800
just do the smallest version of that.

3130
01:56:47.800 --> 01:56:50.140
Yeah, what would the good version of myself do?

3131
01:56:50.140 --> 01:56:53.248
And as heavy as that phone is or whatever it is,

3132
01:56:53.248 --> 01:56:54.081
you know, how difficult it is,

3133
01:56:54.081 --> 01:56:55.698
if you can just do that one thing

3134
01:56:55.698 --> 01:56:57.810
and you're like, wow, I did that and I didn't die.

3135
01:56:57.810 --> 01:56:58.773
Yeah.
Right.

3136
01:56:59.650 --> 01:57:01.310
I think the other thing is

3137
01:57:02.390 --> 01:57:06.400
to reframe this word failure

3138
01:57:06.400 --> 01:57:08.400
and recast it as learning,

3139
01:57:08.400 --> 01:57:10.360
like I don't know what this failure,

3140
01:57:10.360 --> 01:57:13.120
colossal type of failure is, specifically again,

3141
01:57:13.120 --> 01:57:15.090
that you're experiencing,

3142
01:57:15.090 --> 01:57:20.090
but can we look at it instead as a learning experience?

3143
01:57:20.310 --> 01:57:22.813
Like what can be gleaned from whatever it is

3144
01:57:22.813 --> 01:57:25.710
that you're going through that you can then leverage

3145
01:57:25.710 --> 01:57:28.210
to be better and grow?

3146
01:57:28.210 --> 01:57:32.640
And I think in truth, success is about failure.

3147
01:57:32.640 --> 01:57:37.370
There isn't success that exists outside of failure.

3148
01:57:37.370 --> 01:57:39.790
Success is about trying.

3149
01:57:39.790 --> 01:57:41.650
It's about not being afraid to fail

3150
01:57:41.650 --> 01:57:44.280
and not taking failures personally.

3151
01:57:44.280 --> 01:57:48.370
And the thing that you're attempting to do

3152
01:57:48.370 --> 01:57:49.880
may have failed but it's important

3153
01:57:49.880 --> 01:57:51.470
to depersonalize yourself from that.

3154
01:57:51.470 --> 01:57:52.900
You didn't fail.

3155
01:57:52.900 --> 01:57:54.183
This thing failed.

3156
01:57:55.020 --> 01:57:56.400
You had the courage to try.

3157
01:57:56.400 --> 01:57:59.550
So can you disassociate your identity,

3158
01:57:59.550 --> 01:58:00.940
your sense of self,

3159
01:58:00.940 --> 01:58:03.530
from the thing itself so that your identity

3160
01:58:03.530 --> 01:58:05.810
isn't tied up in how the thing does,

3161
01:58:05.810 --> 01:58:07.350
if that makes sense, right?

3162
01:58:07.350 --> 01:58:09.130
That way you create a little bit of distance

3163
01:58:09.130 --> 01:58:14.130
between yourself, your identity and your actions.

3164
01:58:14.270 --> 01:58:15.880
And at the same time,

3165
01:58:15.880 --> 01:58:20.470
keep showing up at the plate and, you know, swing the bat.

3166
01:58:20.470 --> 01:58:24.000
Because if there's one trait that successful people share,

3167
01:58:24.000 --> 01:58:28.550
it's that they fail way more than they succeed.

3168
01:58:28.550 --> 01:58:32.380
They just try so often and so regularly

3169
01:58:32.380 --> 01:58:33.870
and we forget about the failures,

3170
01:58:33.870 --> 01:58:35.120
we only see the successes.

3171
01:58:35.120 --> 01:58:38.810
And this is another message or theme of Adam Grant's work.

3172
01:58:38.810 --> 01:58:42.063
Like his book "Originals" was all about this.

3173
01:58:42.063 --> 01:58:43.680
Like what makes people originals?

3174
01:58:43.680 --> 01:58:45.710
And he looks at all these successful people

3175
01:58:45.710 --> 01:58:48.330
and realizes like, these people failed all the time,

3176
01:58:48.330 --> 01:58:50.102
whether it's Picasso

3177
01:58:50.102 --> 01:58:54.450
or Edison, like they have tons of failures in their wakes.

3178
01:58:54.450 --> 01:58:56.170
And we don't look at those or think about those.

3179
01:58:56.170 --> 01:58:58.980
We just focus on the few successes they had

3180
01:58:58.980 --> 01:59:02.260
but they took more bats at plate than anybody else.

3181
01:59:02.260 --> 01:59:05.240
So if you can reframe this whole thing

3182
01:59:05.240 --> 01:59:07.240
from that perspective,

3183
01:59:07.240 --> 01:59:10.830
that might make it easier to get back up to the plate

3184
01:59:10.830 --> 01:59:12.050
and swing again.

3185
01:59:12.050 --> 01:59:15.670
And really try to objectively deconstruct

3186
01:59:15.670 --> 01:59:18.220
what you're going through and find the lessons in there.

3187
01:59:18.220 --> 01:59:20.410
And if you can do that

3188
01:59:20.410 --> 01:59:24.510
and start figuring out how to implement those lessons

3189
01:59:24.510 --> 01:59:26.770
to craft a better version of yourself,

3190
01:59:26.770 --> 01:59:28.510
five years from now, you could look back on

3191
01:59:28.510 --> 01:59:30.390
whatever it is you're going through right now and say,

3192
01:59:30.390 --> 01:59:32.270
that was the best thing that ever happened to me.

3193
01:59:32.270 --> 01:59:34.150
And that sounds glib.

3194
01:59:34.150 --> 01:59:35.820
And I don't mean to be insensitive

3195
01:59:35.820 --> 01:59:37.270
to what you're going through,

3196
01:59:37.270 --> 01:59:39.720
but I've heard this, I've experienced this myself.

3197
01:59:39.720 --> 01:59:41.520
And I know so many other people that have

3198
01:59:41.520 --> 01:59:44.950
and maybe that'll provide you with a little sliver of hope

3199
01:59:44.950 --> 01:59:48.700
to dig a little bit deeper to get yourself out of this hole.

3200
01:59:48.700 --> 01:59:50.240
Yeah.

3201
01:59:50.240 --> 01:59:52.130
When I hear his message,

3202
01:59:52.130 --> 01:59:55.807
I think of myself, 40 years old, marriage fell apart,

3203
01:59:55.807 --> 01:59:58.820
"Lonely Planet" jobs like going away,

3204
01:59:58.820 --> 02:00:00.730
because maybe "Lonely Planet" is failing.

3205
02:00:00.730 --> 02:00:02.500
That was what was happening then.

3206
02:00:02.500 --> 02:00:05.330
And that was the worry, then, didn't fail.

3207
02:00:05.330 --> 02:00:07.940
But I saw all my income going away

3208
02:00:07.940 --> 02:00:11.320
which wasn't that huge of an income anyway.

3209
02:00:11.320 --> 02:00:14.250
I saw my identity as a travel writer, adventurer,

3210
02:00:14.250 --> 02:00:15.083
going away.

3211
02:00:15.083 --> 02:00:18.250
I didn't have the life I thought I'd had.

3212
02:00:18.250 --> 02:00:19.887
And then that was just the beginning of like,

3213
02:00:19.887 --> 02:00:22.080
it seemed like everything was working against me,

3214
02:00:22.080 --> 02:00:24.060
just like one thing after another.

3215
02:00:24.060 --> 02:00:25.570
And it's hard not to take things personally

3216
02:00:25.570 --> 02:00:26.710
when it just keeps,

3217
02:00:26.710 --> 02:00:28.993
you just feel like you're in a vicious cycle.

3218
02:00:30.398 --> 02:00:33.070
And so I totally feel that.

3219
02:00:33.070 --> 02:00:35.170
And I know how that can, I know how that is.

3220
02:00:35.170 --> 02:00:37.563
So, you know, the only thing is,

3221
02:00:37.563 --> 02:00:40.700
it's like weather, eventually that luck turns,

3222
02:00:40.700 --> 02:00:42.760
especially if you take these small steps,

3223
02:00:42.760 --> 02:00:43.720
like Rich laid out.

3224
02:00:43.720 --> 02:00:46.340
I would add just like, sometimes it helps,

3225
02:00:46.340 --> 02:00:49.190
if in the morning you could do one thing physically

3226
02:00:49.190 --> 02:00:51.080
that is not,

3227
02:00:51.080 --> 02:00:54.220
whether it's do 10 sun salutations

3228
02:00:54.220 --> 02:00:57.970
or sit down and try to meditate for five or 10 minutes

3229
02:00:57.970 --> 02:00:59.500
and turn your brain off, if you can.

3230
02:00:59.500 --> 02:01:00.670
I mean, it's hard to at first,

3231
02:01:00.670 --> 02:01:03.380
but like, one physical thing you can do,

3232
02:01:03.380 --> 02:01:04.450
first thing in the morning,

3233
02:01:04.450 --> 02:01:05.770
right when you get up.

3234
02:01:05.770 --> 02:01:08.150
So at least that time, right after that,

3235
02:01:08.150 --> 02:01:11.020
you kind of feel good.
Yeah, a little self care.

3236
02:01:11.020 --> 02:01:12.650
Just a little bit.

3237
02:01:12.650 --> 02:01:14.073
And to quote, Karamo,

3238
02:01:15.150 --> 02:01:19.170
can you look at this as something that is happening

3239
02:01:19.170 --> 02:01:20.897
not to you, but for you?

3240
02:01:20.897 --> 02:01:22.430
And that's beautiful, I love that,

3241
02:01:22.430 --> 02:01:23.332
yeah, I love that.

3242
02:01:23.332 --> 02:01:25.030
And I say that you have your version of this story.

3243
02:01:25.030 --> 02:01:28.050
Look, you know, I've hit bottom as an alcoholic.

3244
02:01:28.050 --> 02:01:29.350
I've been unemployable.

3245
02:01:29.350 --> 02:01:30.460
I've been in a situation

3246
02:01:30.460 --> 02:01:32.350
where my family didn't want anything to do with me.

3247
02:01:32.350 --> 02:01:33.750
I've had cars repossessed.

3248
02:01:33.750 --> 02:01:34.840
I almost lost my house.

3249
02:01:34.840 --> 02:01:36.500
I've been unable to pay my bill.

3250
02:01:36.500 --> 02:01:39.890
I've had so many, you know, versions of

3251
02:01:40.900 --> 02:01:42.450
feeling like a failure

3252
02:01:43.500 --> 02:01:45.610
and have been able to claw out of it.

3253
02:01:45.610 --> 02:01:48.370
So I don't know what John's circumstances are

3254
02:01:48.370 --> 02:01:51.930
but I do believe and trust that no matter where he is,

3255
02:01:51.930 --> 02:01:53.310
there is a better place for him.

3256
02:01:53.310 --> 02:01:55.900
And there's always light at the end of the tunnel.

3257
02:01:55.900 --> 02:01:56.733
There you go.

3258
02:01:58.000 --> 02:02:01.530
All right, one last one from Phoenix, Arizona.

3259
02:02:01.530 --> 02:02:02.940
Hi, my name is Sarah

3260
02:02:02.940 --> 02:02:05.500
and I live in Phoenix, Arizona.

3261
02:02:05.500 --> 02:02:08.730
And I'm wondering if you're willing to discuss

3262
02:02:08.730 --> 02:02:11.970
just something interesting that I've noticed.

3263
02:02:11.970 --> 02:02:14.040
So I'm in my first year of sobriety

3264
02:02:14.040 --> 02:02:16.510
after a long struggle with drugs and alcohol.

3265
02:02:16.510 --> 02:02:19.380
I am a long-time athlete playing lots of sports

3266
02:02:19.380 --> 02:02:21.100
and loving running.

3267
02:02:21.100 --> 02:02:24.260
And I was wondering if you were willing to discuss

3268
02:02:24.260 --> 02:02:29.260
how overcoming substance abuse has changed your mindset

3269
02:02:30.440 --> 02:02:35.440
on fitness, your life, your goals, your athleticism,

3270
02:02:35.640 --> 02:02:36.820
just things like that.

3271
02:02:36.820 --> 02:02:38.570
I'm a huge fan of the show

3272
02:02:38.570 --> 02:02:42.640
and I'm super happy to even reach out,

3273
02:02:42.640 --> 02:02:44.200
but hopefully, you'll

3274
02:02:46.190 --> 02:02:48.440
address these kinds of things in the talk

3275
02:02:48.440 --> 02:02:50.730
because your story is really powerful.

3276
02:02:50.730 --> 02:02:53.240
And I think it would empower a lot of other people

3277
02:02:54.080 --> 02:02:57.330
to take hold of their life, their bodies, their fitness.

3278
02:02:57.330 --> 02:02:58.163
Thanks again.

3279
02:02:58.163 --> 02:03:01.200
And I hope that y'all are having a wonderful day.

3280
02:03:01.200 --> 02:03:04.930
Cool, thanks for the questions, Sarah.

3281
02:03:04.930 --> 02:03:09.600
Congrats on a year of sobriety, that's a huge deal.

3282
02:03:09.600 --> 02:03:12.490
Amazing and it's a great question.

3283
02:03:12.490 --> 02:03:13.440
It's an interesting question.

3284
02:03:13.440 --> 02:03:15.780
I mean, the first thing I would say is,

3285
02:03:15.780 --> 02:03:17.830
sobriety first.

3286
02:03:17.830 --> 02:03:20.010
Like, don't be confused.

3287
02:03:20.010 --> 02:03:23.520
Like, there is a confused narrative out there

3288
02:03:26.180 --> 02:03:28.560
that somehow like being vegan

3289
02:03:28.560 --> 02:03:30.140
or being an athlete

3290
02:03:30.140 --> 02:03:33.610
contributed to me getting sober and staying sober.

3291
02:03:33.610 --> 02:03:35.940
And that's just not what happened at all.

3292
02:03:35.940 --> 02:03:37.770
Like, I didn't get and stay sober

3293
02:03:37.770 --> 02:03:41.230
because I went vegan or became an endurance athlete,

3294
02:03:41.230 --> 02:03:46.230
I got and stayed sober by overcoming denial,

3295
02:03:46.360 --> 02:03:47.540
finding people to talK to,

3296
02:03:47.540 --> 02:03:49.340
being honest, holding myself accountable,

3297
02:03:49.340 --> 02:03:52.930
working a program in the secret rooms

3298
02:03:52.930 --> 02:03:56.090
and helping others and working with a sponsor

3299
02:03:56.090 --> 02:03:59.040
and doing an inventory and making amends.

3300
02:03:59.040 --> 02:04:00.980
And it's really only when

3301
02:04:00.980 --> 02:04:03.810
I created a solid foundation of sobriety

3302
02:04:03.810 --> 02:04:06.500
that I began to expand in other areas

3303
02:04:06.500 --> 02:04:08.150
like being vegan and becoming

3304
02:04:08.150 --> 02:04:10.030
this middle-aged endurance athlete,

3305
02:04:10.030 --> 02:04:11.430
came many years after.

3306
02:04:11.430 --> 02:04:12.710
I got sober at 31.

3307
02:04:12.710 --> 02:04:15.970
I didn't start doing Ultras until I was 42.

3308
02:04:15.970 --> 02:04:18.610
I got, you know, I went vegan at 40.

3309
02:04:18.610 --> 02:04:22.010
So there's a decade after getting sober

3310
02:04:22.010 --> 02:04:24.160
where I was trying to sort my shit out

3311
02:04:24.160 --> 02:04:25.690
and get my life back on track

3312
02:04:25.690 --> 02:04:27.240
before any of these other things.

3313
02:04:27.240 --> 02:04:30.860
So this idea, this notion that addictive personality

3314
02:04:30.860 --> 02:04:34.230
can just go from one thing to then you can put an athlete,

3315
02:04:34.230 --> 02:04:36.470
you can make them an athlete instead, and he can channel.

3316
02:04:36.470 --> 02:04:37.670
And that compensates.

3317
02:04:37.670 --> 02:04:38.503
I mean, you could.

3318
02:04:38.503 --> 02:04:40.430
It's just, that's not how it played out for me.

3319
02:04:40.430 --> 02:04:42.600
Like I had a decade of, you know,

3320
02:04:42.600 --> 02:04:45.250
being a workaholic and like eating shitty food.

3321
02:04:45.250 --> 02:04:47.340
I transferred many addictive tendencies

3322
02:04:47.340 --> 02:04:50.430
on to other things that weren't drugs or alcohol.

3323
02:04:50.430 --> 02:04:53.180
And it took me a long time in my spiritual evolution

3324
02:04:53.180 --> 02:04:54.750
to like grapple with those things.

3325
02:04:54.750 --> 02:04:57.250
And as they say, the road gets narrower.

3326
02:04:57.250 --> 02:05:00.120
Like when you first get sober,

3327
02:05:00.120 --> 02:05:03.640
just to not drink, is everything, right?

3328
02:05:03.640 --> 02:05:04.870
Anything else is fine.

3329
02:05:04.870 --> 02:05:06.490
It's just like, just don't drink, right?

3330
02:05:06.490 --> 02:05:09.610
And then the more emotionally sober you get,

3331
02:05:09.610 --> 02:05:13.340
the less tolerant you become of other behaviors

3332
02:05:13.340 --> 02:05:16.120
and proclivities that you have that used to not bother you.

3333
02:05:16.120 --> 02:05:18.440
Like, you just can't get away with it anymore

3334
02:05:18.440 --> 02:05:21.660
because the more emotionally sober and mature you become,

3335
02:05:21.660 --> 02:05:23.680
you realize that those things are at odds

3336
02:05:23.680 --> 02:05:26.450
with you being the most, you know,

3337
02:05:26.450 --> 02:05:27.930
actualized person that you can be.

3338
02:05:27.930 --> 02:05:29.910
So whether it's, you know,

3339
02:05:29.910 --> 02:05:33.350
going to gamble or shopping too much

3340
02:05:33.350 --> 02:05:36.320
or working whatever, you know, shitty self-care habits,

3341
02:05:36.320 --> 02:05:39.770
whatever it is, like those things become,

3342
02:05:39.770 --> 02:05:40.760
if you get sober enough,

3343
02:05:40.760 --> 02:05:43.230
they become unbearable and they have to go, as well.

3344
02:05:43.230 --> 02:05:45.220
And this is, it's called slowbriety.

3345
02:05:45.220 --> 02:05:47.200
It takes a long time.

3346
02:05:47.200 --> 02:05:50.900
So in my case, these things didn't happen in lockstep.

3347
02:05:50.900 --> 02:05:54.640
And so I just wanna impress upon anybody who's listening

3348
02:05:54.640 --> 02:05:58.090
to understand that things like, you know,

3349
02:05:58.090 --> 02:06:00.970
